-<section id="rta-review-checkpoint"><h2>Separate RTA verifier: fixed review checkpoint</h2><p>The <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-rta-reference/blob/a839d7a918c9a23ce170937f536e6c13b3a69b93/docs/REPRODUCTION_CHECKPOINT_2026-10-26.md">VCP RTA review instructions</a> fix the target at <code>cc695fe</code>. This is a first-party PoC with legacy v1.1-labelled evidence, separate from the illustrative examples on this page, the VCP v1.2 candidate checker and the earlier VAP reproduction kit. It is not a native VCP/VAP conformance verifier.</p><p>The ordinary CLI reports VALID, INVALID and INDETERMINATE using a caller-supplied trusted key. A separate opt-in command verifies signed supplemental records and offline RFC 3161 timestamps; that supplemental format remains unadopted. A later timestamp does not establish the original log or anchor time.</p><p>The historical corpus contains 20 SIG and 20 EXE events. Legacy hash, signature and Merkle comparisons match selected reference material, but the first PrevHash boundary, authenticated batch metadata and original external anchor remain unresolved. The expected overall verdict is INDETERMINATE (replay exit code 2), not full evidence acceptance. Internal tests succeeded at 809 regression and 15 separate historical cases per recorded environment; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p>The recorded CI used temporary merge 0314e01 with the same Git tree as target cc695fe; these are different commits. The later guide is a839d7a. Retain failures, environment differences and assistance; keep publication permissions separate. Original Actions artifact retention is 30 days; selected JSON copies are now also in Git, as explained below and the environment is not fully locked. This website update reports the records; it is not another verifier run. <a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-26-rta-verifier-checkpoint/">Read the announcement and source records →</a></p></section><p><strong>Follow-up: complete recipe exercised by first-party CI.</strong> <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-rta-reference/pull/16">PR #16</a> adds a separate workflow maintained by the same project. <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-rta-reference/actions/runs/40263948191">Its two successful Python jobs</a> run the exact published recipe from a fresh public clone, create a virtual environment, install dependencies, compare 29 inputs, execute the fixed 809 + 15 cases and assess the INDETERMINATE replay. The launcher’s 13 synthetic unit tests are separate; these repeated checkpoint cases do not add new unique coverage. The automation revision differs from the pinned guide and checkpoint. See the <a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-rta-reference/blob/4a40ee40f44ca8efe1e4d4f0f07df9050d5f3b21/docs/CHECKPOINT_RECIPE_CI.md">scope and retained reports</a>. The workflow is not a general sandbox or an independent third-party result.</p><section id="records-and-review-intake" class="evidence" style="scroll-margin-top:8rem"><h2>26 October update: selected original CI records and review intake</h2><p>Six selected original JSON files from the completed first-party CI (three per Python environment) are now stored in Git: the procedure-completion record, final assessment and original artifact manifest. They are byte-for-byte copies, not another execution. Full JUnit XML, the detailed 40-event replay and shell logs are not included. The selected copies no longer depend solely on the Actions artifact’s 30-day retention, but Git availability is not immutable or guaranteed permanent storage. Hashes of omitted files cannot recover their bytes.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-rta-reference/blob/ec424de00f7c4b59506f173eca000f8faaacf71a/docs/reproduction-results/2026-10-26-pr16/README.md">Selected original CI records and their limits</a></p><p>The review intake distinguishes the RTA checkpoint (target cc695fe, guide a839d7a) from the VAP OS-isolated mock-gate kit (kit b1af0dc, target c8ccf97). Acceptance of one assignment does not authorize substituting the other. Willingness to run, receipt of a report, technical agreement, independence and publication permission are separate states. Preserve failures, incomplete runs, environment differences and assistance. Permission for results, raw logs, name, affiliation and specific attribution must be checked separately.</p><p>GitHub issues are public, including the submitting account and attachments. For a private technical report, first contact standards@veritaschain.org to agree a transfer method, without attaching secrets. A template, closed issue or successful first-party CI does not establish independent reproduction. The experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction remains unestablished.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/veritaschain/vcp-rta-reference/blob/ec424de00f7c4b59506f173eca000f8faaacf71a/docs/EXTERNAL_REVIEW_INTAKE.md">Review targets and submission guidance</a></p></section><section class="status"><h2>Published research and verification</h2><p>Find evidence verification, cloud credentials, payment authorization, VCP integrity research and SDK resources. Extensions remain unadopted; independent reproduction is not established.</p><p><a href="/research/">Browse research resources →</a></p></section>
